# SRG-APP-000370-AU-000260  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to generate reports that do not
# alter original content or time ordering of log records.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000370-AU-000260
group:           V-206503
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001882
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    A Splunk report is a search over indexed events, so the application
                 decides whether the report presents the record as stored. The product
                 exposes settings that do alter presented content - search-time field
                 filters, index-time sed scripts, and search commands that rewrite values -
                 and the application's share is that none of them is applied to the audit
                 data a report reads.

governs:         props.conf - How incoming data is recognized, parsed and timestamped.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           field_filters.conf [<fieldFilterName>] action absent
check:           props.conf [<spec>] SEDCMD-<class> absent
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether a report as rendered preserves content and time ordering is
                 confirmed by comparing report output with the stored records, which the
                 assessor performs.
external:        Handling of an exported report after it leaves the application - a PDF or
                 CSV passed on, edited or re-sorted downstream - rests on the recipient's
                 procedures.

citation:        field_filters.conf.spec:32 [<fieldFilterName>], :37-70 action = <field> =
                 <operator> with the operator vocabulary null() | sha256() | sha512() |
                 <string literal> | sed(<string literal>); props.conf.spec:80 [<spec>],
                 :1243 SEDCMD-<class>; savedsearches.conf.spec:44 search.
finding:         Assessed at the application layer alone: a field filter, a SEDCMD class or
                 a content-rewriting search command is applied to the audit data a report
                 reads, so the report does not present the original content of the log
                 records.
